{
  "title": "THA Trunnionosis",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/recon/422821/tha-trunnionosis",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Mar 26 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Trunnionosis is also referred to as Mechanically assisted crevice corrosion (MACC)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "THA Trunnionosis is a complication of hip arthroplasty caused by metal ion release from corrosion at the femoral head-neck interface morse taper leading to hip pain and adverse local tissue reactions.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be suspected in a patient with elevated serum metal ions with cobalt levels being elevated more substantially than chromium levels. MRI studies can be helpful to assess for pseudotumors.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is observation for patients without symptoms. Single stage revision THA is indicated for patients with a painful THA in the absence of an infection.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "modular designs",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "large cobalt chrome femoral heads",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "larger heads may put more torsional forces on the trunnion.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "taper design",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "shorter taper length may afford less interference fit and more micromotion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**greater rigidity** of the taper may lead to less wear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "metal on metal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "serum metal ions may contribute to taper wear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "no pathognomonic serum metal ion level for trunnionosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "serum cobalt >1 ng/ml (ppb) should lead to consideration for mechanically assisted crevice corrosion (MACC)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "mixed alloy components",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Galvanic corrosion**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "corrosion caused by an electrochemical transfer of electrons between dissimilar metals",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "i.e. cobalt-chromium (CoCr) alloy femoral head on a titanium alloy stem",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**Fretting corrosion**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422821/images/trunnion_wear.jpg",
                  "caption": "Photograph demonstrating trunnion wear"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "corrosion from relative micromotion between two materials causing wear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "i.e. tolerance between male and female morse taper allows for micromotion and wear",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "contributes to **trunniononsis**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**Crevice corrosion**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "physicochemical interaction between a metal and environment leading to altered mehcanical properties",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "stainless steel most prone to crevice corrosion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The adverse reaction to metal debris generation may result in an aseptic lymphocyte-dominant vasculitis association lesion (ALVAL; also referred to as pseudotumor) similar to that seen in metal-on-metal hips",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain and limp are the most common complaints",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "occasionally if ALTR is large enough a palpable pseudocyst can be felt",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "abduction weakness if ALTR has caused soft tissue destruction of abductors",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "AP and lateral hip views should be obtained",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "imaging studies may be normal in the setting of trunnnionosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Judet views and/or CT scan may be obtained if advanced osteolysis is present",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "MARS MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422821/images/pseudotumor.jpg",
              "caption": "MARS MRI showing an example of a pseudotumor following ALTR"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "findings may include periarticular pseudotumors and/or soft tissue destruction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Infection should be ruled out",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "ESR, CRP, WBC",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Aspiration",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "consider manual cell count as metal debris can cause a false elevation of automated cell count",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Metal ion levels",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "cobalt and chromium ion levels",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**cobalt levels are elevated substantially more than chromium levels**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "ratio of at least 2:1 encountered when caused by head-neck junction trunnionosis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "ratio of 1:1 is suggestive of metal-on-metal implant wear",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "revision total hip",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "painful THA with the above risk factors and elevated serum cobalt level compared to serum chromium level elevation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "frozen-sections and intraoperative cultures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "extensive synovectomy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "inspection of the taper and decision for retention of stem versus revision stem",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422821/images/trunnionosis_example_2.jpg",
                          "caption": "Example of trunnionosis of the taper and cobalt chrome head"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "to **ceramic head with titanium sleeve and new polyethylene liner**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
